# Closed-class words that never stand as a counted noun right after an hour:
# pronouns, adverbs and verb particles ("a las 8 te llamo").  Each word's class
# is quoted from its Wiktionary entry (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the
# fetched pages are kept with the audit.  Markup is removed from the quotes.
# me: Pronoun. "The first-person singular, as the object (of a verb, preposition, etc)."
# you: Pronoun. "(object pronoun) The people spoken, or written to, as an object."
# him: Pronoun. "A masculine pronoun; he as a grammatical object."
# her: Pronoun. "The form of she used after a preposition, as the object of a verb, or (colloquial) as a subject with a conj..."
# us: Pronoun. "Me and at least one other person, excluding the person(s) being addressed. (exclusive us.)"
# them: Pronoun. "(in the plural) Those ones."
# it: Pronoun. "The third-person singular neuter personal pronoun used to refer to an inanimate object, abstract entity, or..."
# home: Adverb. "To one's home."
# back: Adverb. "(not comparable) To or in a previous condition or place."
# away: Adverb. "From a place, hence."
# out: Adverb. "Away from the inside or centre."
me
you
him
her
us
them
it
home
back
away
out
